invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_blocks.c
catches: rsa_blocks_equiv_test
reason: the square's reduction drops the carry out of word i + k of row i,
  which the next row adds a word higher, so the result is short by a
  multiple of a power of two whenever a row carries out of its top word.
  bin/rsa_blocks_equiv_test holds the square to the blocks' multiplication
  of a by itself and to rsa_mont64.c's loops.

--- old
        ct_u128 sum = (ct_u128)t[i + k] + w + top;
--- new
        ct_u128 sum = (ct_u128)t[i + k] + w + (top & 0);
